        <h4>How to test a PowerVar (UPS):</h4>
        <ol>
            <li>Make sure the PowerVar is plugged into a wall outlet</li>
            <li>Remove the faceplate and verify that the black and red cables are connected. </li>
            <li>Red should connect to red, and black should connect to black.</li>
            <li>Next, press and hold the test button beneath the indicator lights for a few seconds.</li>
            <li>Once you’ve held it long enough, you should hear a beep.</li>
            <li>
                All four indicators should show solid green, indicating that the internal battery is
                functioning properly.
            </li>
        </ol>
        <hr />
        <h4>How to tell that the PowerVar battery is faulty:</h4>
        <p>Make sure the PowerVar is plugged into a wall outlet.</p>
        <p>If you see the fualt light and the battery light blinking on the PowerVar, which indicates the following:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>The internal battery connector cables are not connected to the PowerVar connector cables.</li>
            <li>The internal battery is malfunctioning and needs to be swapped out.</li>
        </ol>
        <hr />
        <h4>How to connect the internal battery connector cables to the PowerVar:</h4>
        <ol>
            <li>Turn off the PowerVar by pressing the power button on the front of the faceplate. If there is no faceplate, the powerbutton is the second button below the indicator lights.</li>
            <li>Remove the faceplate from the front of the PowerVar, and you will see the black and red connector cables.</li>
            <li>Ensure the cables are connected correctly.</li>
            <li>The cables connect as follows: <b class="labelColor-2">RED</b> to <b class="labelColor-2">RED</b> AND <b>BLACK</b> to <b>BLACK</b>.</li>
            <li>If you connect <b class="labelColor-2">RED</b> to <b>BLACK</b>, the device will malfunction and require replacement of the Powervar.</li>
            <li>Once complete, reattach the faceplate and press the power button to turn on the PowerVar.</li>
        </ol>

        <hr/> 

        <h4>How to replace the internal battery for the PowerVar:</h4>
        <li>You can retrieve a replacement battery by buying one from Batteries Plus and from Amazon. </li>
        <li>The battery model is ML7-12 - 12 Volt 7.2 AH, F1 Terminal, Rechargeable SLA AGM Battery also you’ll need electrical tape and scissors.</li>
        <br/>

        <ol>
            <li>Turn off the PowerVar by pressing the power button on the front of the faceplate. If there is no faceplate, the power button is the second button below the indicator lights. </li>
            <li>Remove the faceplate from the front of the PowerVar, and disconnect the <b class="labelColor-2">RED</b> and <b>BLACK</b> cables.</li>
            <li>Unscrew the battery plate covering the battery</li>
            <ul><li>To remove the screws you can use a flat-head screwdriver and/or slip joint pliers.</li></ul>
            <ul><li>Some battery plates have different screws which will require a Phillips head screw driver and/or slip joint pliers.</li></ul>
            <li>Once the battery plate is removed. Remove the battery and disconnect the <b class="labelColor-2">RED</b> and <b>BLACK</b> cable from the battery.</li>
            <li>Once the battery is removed, remove the <b class="labelColor-2">RED</b> and <b>BLACK</b> cables from the used battery; please put the used battery in a box and take it to Batteries Plus for recycling.</li>
            <li>With the new battery place the <b class="labelColor-2">RED</b> cable on the <b class="labelColor-2">RED</b> positive port and the <b>BLACK</b> cable on the <b>BLACK</b> negative port.</li>
            <li>Once the cables are attached to the battery add electrical tape to the positive and negative ports</li>
            <li>You’ll now insert the new battery into the PowerVar.</li>
            <li>After this is complete reattach the battery plate and connect the <b class="labelColor-2">RED</b> connector on the PowerVar to the <b class="labelColor-2">RED</b> connector attached to the internal battery and connect the <b>BLACK</b> connector on the PowerVar to the <b>BLACK</b> connector attached to the internal battery.</li>
            <li>After that is complete attach the face plate if your PowerVar has one. </li>
            <li>Once that is complete plug the power cord for the PowerVar to a wall outlet and press and gold the power button until you hear a beep.</li>
            <li>You should see a solid green light after press the power button indicating that theinternal battery and PowerVar are working correctly.</li>
            <li>If no lights come on or the lights come on and start to flicker the PowerVar is faulty and not the internal battery. Order a replacement through UIS Support at 770-729-5933 option 3.</li>
        </ol>


